It seems like just changing `#include <stdint.h>` to `#include <cstdint>` fixes it?

```c
extern "C" {
#include <cstdint>
int main() { return 42; }
}
```
This compiles fine with `clang++ -c -fcxx-modules -fmodules demo.cpp`.

*Edit:* The problem with this approach is that it doesn't work for C code, so for upstream it would need to be something like:
```cpp
#ifdef __cplusplus
#include <cstdint>
#else
#include <stdint.h>
#endif
```

But I still haven't dived in the docs yet to understand *why* this is now a problem with recent Clang and `-fmodules` that upstream projects may want to care about.
